# A path among the operands is one value whatever its depth: `mytest\x + 2` -- two segments, a
# method-occurrence root -- is read by the general path walk, as `v: mytest\x` and `m\in\x + 1`
# are; no reading by atom count (the author, 2026-10-17: one general algorithm for every path).
# 5 + 2 = 7; 81 is the program's own refusal.
fn: mytest () int
    int: x 5
    return: x
end: mytest
fn: check () int
    int: v
    mytest()
    v: mytest\x + 2
    if: v != 7
        return: 81
    return: v
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
